WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.020
In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Peace and blessings be upon the most noble of creation and messengers, our Prophet Muhammad, upon him be the best prayer and complete peace.

00:08.640 --> 00:13.560
Peace be upon you and the mercy of God and His blessings. Welcome, our colleagues, to this fellowship.

00:14.100 --> 00:18.080
In this explanation, we are not just going to sit and speak some information and words.

00:18.080 --> 00:26.820
We want to draw a map together so that we can know how to leave a real and tangible health impact in our communities and neighborhoods.

00:26.820 --> 00:31.820
Enough of the introductions for now, let us enter directly into the subject and start right now.

00:31.820 --> 00:36.820
There is a question that always poses itself and makes us pause to reflect on our entire healthcare system.

00:36.820 --> 00:43.820
Could it be that doctors and nurses inside clinics and hospitals alone are responsible for protecting our families and community?

00:43.820 --> 00:48.820
Meaning, does health begin and end at the hospital door?

00:48.820 --> 00:55.820
Let us enter this exact scene: We are in the middle of August, a very hot and harsh heatwave strikes our region.

00:55.820 --> 01:00.820
Suddenly, the clinics and hospitals in our neighborhood get overcrowded and completely exhausted.

01:00.820 --> 01:09.820
Emergencies and difficult conditions, most of them elderly people and small children suffering from the lethal heat, heat stress, and dehydration.

01:09.820 --> 01:13.820
Could we have prevented these conditions from the beginning?

01:13.820 --> 01:23.820
Practically, yes. Statistically, two-thirds of these conditions could have been avoided and prevented entirely, sparing all these hospital beds and pain.

01:23.820 --> 01:25.820
If someone had gone down, for example, a day or two earlier.

01:25.820 --> 01:29.820
And shared with people three simple steps:

01:29.820 --> 01:31.820
To drink water before we feel thirsty.

01:31.820 --> 01:36.820
To stay away from the sun during peak heat from 12:00 PM to 4:00 PM.

01:36.820 --> 01:39.820
And to check on elderly neighbors to reassure ourselves about them.

01:39.820 --> 01:44.820
And right here comes the role of the community health educator.

01:44.820 --> 01:53.820
The community health educator is the person who helps community members understand health information and use it to make better decisions for their health.

01:53.820 --> 01:55.820
They do not diagnose diseases, nor do they prescribe medications.

01:55.820 --> 01:58.820
Nor do they place themselves in the position of a doctor or a nurse.

01:58.820 --> 02:04.820
They are the connecting link and the essential human bridge between medical knowledge and the community.

02:04.820 --> 02:13.820
They take complex medical science and simplify it into easy and understandable steps so that people can apply them in their daily lives.

02:13.820 --> 02:19.820
Many problems we can halt and prevent before they unravel and reach the hospital door.

02:19.820 --> 02:25.820
Things like smoking, obesity, lack of physical activity and movement.

02:25.820 --> 02:28.820
Infectious diseases, mental health problems.

02:28.820 --> 02:32.820
All of these are influenced by people's awareness, behaviors, and habits.

02:32.820 --> 02:36.820
And here health education becomes the foundation.

02:36.820 --> 02:40.820
So instead of sitting and waiting for disease to occur, we work on preventing it.

02:40.820 --> 02:44.820
And instead of continuing to treat the problem after the damage is already done.

02:44.820 --> 02:47.820
We help people avoid it from its roots and from its very beginning.

02:47.820 --> 02:50.820
The community health educator carries out four primary missions:

02:50.820 --> 02:53.820
First, disseminating health awareness.

02:53.820 --> 02:55.820
Simplifying difficult medical information.

02:55.820 --> 02:57.820
And complex scientific knowledge.

02:57.820 --> 03:00.820
Supporting and encouraging positive health behaviors.

03:00.820 --> 03:06.820
And linking people and the community to available medical resources and services to benefit them.

03:06.820 --> 03:08.820
Their work is active in the field.

03:08.820 --> 03:10.820
Not sitting waiting for anyone.

03:10.820 --> 03:11.820
They go into schools.

03:11.820 --> 03:12.820
Into universities.

03:12.820 --> 03:13.820
Into associations.

03:13.820 --> 03:14.820
Workshops.

03:14.820 --> 03:15.820
On social media.

03:15.820 --> 03:16.820
And among the people.

03:16.820 --> 03:19.820
And today we are before a new and major challenge.

03:19.820 --> 03:21.820
And it is increasing day by day.

03:21.820 --> 03:23.820
Which is climate change.

03:23.820 --> 03:27.820
Many people think that climate change is just an environmental story.

03:27.820 --> 03:30.820
Meaning even a sad polar bear.

03:30.820 --> 03:33.820
Standing on a melting piece of ice in a far-off location.

03:33.820 --> 03:37.820
Yet the reality is that it is a direct and immediate danger to our health and the health of our children.

03:37.820 --> 03:39.820
Such as intense heatwaves.

03:39.820 --> 03:41.820
Air pollution.

03:41.820 --> 03:43.820
Chest tightness and asthma.

03:43.820 --> 03:46.820
Diseases transmitted by insects and water.

03:46.820 --> 03:47.820
Food security.

03:47.820 --> 03:49.820
And the impact on our psychological health.

03:49.820 --> 03:52.820
For this reason, the community health educator.

03:52.820 --> 03:54.820
Must understand this link properly.

03:54.820 --> 03:58.820
And help their community protect itself in a world whose climate is changing every day.

03:58.820 --> 04:00.820
In summary, colleagues.

04:00.820 --> 04:04.820
The health educator is the bridge between science and the people of the community.

04:04.820 --> 04:06.820
Their role is not merely transferring words and information.

04:06.820 --> 04:10.820
Their role is helping people understand and apply on the ground and change their behavior.

04:10.820 --> 04:12.820
And in a world where climate has an impact.

04:12.820 --> 04:15.820
This role becomes more important than anytime past.

04:15.820 --> 04:18.820
And in the end we want to conclude with this challenge:

04:18.820 --> 04:19.820
Think about it.

04:19.820 --> 04:21.820
Write for us in two or three lines:

04:21.820 --> 04:30.820
How can you, as a health educator, help your neighborhood and community confront one of these health challenges linked to climate change?

04:30.820 --> 04:34.820
Because creating real impact always starts from simple steps.
